-- CMS phase 2: cms_sections rows for every (page, section) introduced by
-- 20260814120000_seed_cms_navbar.sql .. 20260814122100_seed_cms_legal.sql
-- (docs/cms-final-seed.md). One row per section actually rendered on a page;
-- title/anchor/route come from the same docs/cms-keys-*.json metadata used to
-- generate those cms_content rows (membership's own sections are hand-authored,
-- see docs/cms-final-seed.md). sort_order is the section's position on the page,
-- in steps of 10, taken from the lowest sort_order among its fields.
-- ON CONFLICT (page, section_key) DO NOTHING, same reasoning as cms_content:
-- never overwrite a row a client may already be seeing/editing.

ON CONFLICT (page, section_key) DO NOTHING;
